+
+## Native source, display and export follow-up
+
+Each compiled/rendered part now retains its authoritative `TriangleMesh` in
+OpenSCAD Z-up coordinates. The same native source reaches the application and
+export path; derived Bevy buffers remain Y-up display projections. Shared native
+geometry is cloned through its Arc storage, extending its lifetime without
+duplicating coordinate/expression buffers. This increases retained memory; the
+48-byte increase in the part value is not a total retained-heap measurement.
+
+The unchanged near-coincident cylinder fixture reproduces distinct exact
+vertices rounding to equal binary32 display positions. Hypermesh's native GPU
+API constructs finite normals from exact triangles and permits this display
+collapse. SynapsCAD now reuses that API, keeps GPU errors and their typed causes,
+and retains the exact source. The original fifteen-case rotation test passes.
+No display position, normal or index is consumed as source geometry by export.
+
+STL uses the native serializer and rejects binary32 triangle collapse before
+replacing a file. OBJ uses native geometry serialization with application-only
+material/group records. 3MF projects the native source to binary64 and validates
+encoded triangles through the native predicates. Original exact triangles are
+also validated first: the collinear points `(0,0)`, `(1/2,1/5)`, `(3/2,3/5)`
+can appear nondegenerate after rounding. Removing this preflight reproduced
+false export success. Orphan native positions also fail explicitly. Numerical
+conversion/validation errors are returned before file creation; this is not a
+promise of transactional recovery from later filesystem errors.
+
+All three formats ignore edits to display buffers. Tests retain the thin-box
+write/read regressions, native axes and winding, global OBJ indices, source-order
+material ownership, and an exported/reimported two-part model used as a further
+exact Boolean operand (independent volumes 25 then 24).
+
+This is an explicit API/artifact migration: external `MeshData` struct literals
+now need a native `source`; exports use authored Z-up coordinates and native
+winding instead of the previous renderer-buffer convention. OBJ/3MF no longer
+weld renderer copies, OBJ omits derived normal records and requests flat shading,
+and native GPU projection may change display coordinates/normals at float
+rounding boundaries. Cross-revision byte identity is not claimed. Plain format
+files remain lossy, omit native source receipts, and do not certify source
+fidelity or general preservation of topology after projection.
+
+Final focused checks: 43 binary/UI tests and four conversion tests pass;
+warning-denied all-target Clippy, native release build, WASM binary and fuzz-target
+compilation, rustdoc, formatting and whitespace checks pass. The unchanged
+configured CI command terminated with exit 101: 64 passed, one failed, two
+ignored and 53 filtered, in 935.18 seconds. B-text extrusion still times out;
+no fixture, assertion or workflow exclusion was weakened. A separately labelled
+run excluding B for diagnosis passed 64 tests, with two ignored and 54 filtered;
+it is not a passing replacement for the CI command. The configured library
+run predates final test-only/documentation edits; current conversion witnesses
+were rerun, and final export changes have their complete binary test run.
+
+The ordinary through-hole preview matches installed OpenSCAD 2021.01 visually.
+At both tiny rotation angles, OpenSCAD reports a non-manifold result and differs
+visually; images and warnings are retained. General visual conformance, especially
+those degenerate reference cases, is not established.
+
+Cost is adverse: a warm source-carrying shim of the prior normal calculation
+versus the native GPU route measures about 0.006/0.022 ms for a cube, 11.2/83.2 ms
+for a 528-triangle sphere, 0.010/0.051 ms for a drilled body, and 0.248/1.335 ms
+for a rotated cylinder (20 alternating pairs each, one shared-host process).
+These paths have different display outputs and this is a capability migration,
+not a performance-only optimization or a matched end-to-end speedup claim.
+The candidate default scene completes three times in 288–320 ms with 20 parts,
+2,632 native triangles, five views and no failures or warnings. The unchanged
+benchmark driver also completes `default:all` at its default `$fn=16` in a
+single 480 ms smoke run; no paired speedup is inferred. Native normal
+construction/reuse cost remains a research target.
+
+Source retention for models that cannot produce any finite f32 display buffer,
+full projected-topology guarantees, exact native file replay and installed
+distribution remain open. No push is qualified while configured CI fails. The
+CSGRS evidence index retains this follow-up separately from earlier checkpoints.
